From 27cdd504b0977ca464e477356fe3fdf42380c290 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:55:12 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 23/48] I/O: file providers, files the host serves at a guest
 path

hle_extension::add_file_provider (interface version 4) lets a port or a
module serve a file at a guest path: in place of the file there, or where
there is none. Every provider is asked, in order, at each sceIoOpen and
sceIoOpenAsync that only reads, with "disc0:/" or "ms0:/" and the resolved
path, and the descriptor the file there was opened as (0 when there is
none). The first to return a file filter serves the file: the game reads
what the filter gives, as with set_file_filter, and a path with no file
opens as the filter's bytes alone. sceIoGetstat of a path with no file
reports a served file's size. Opens for writing, the raw disc device,
sce_lbn files, directories and the host's own reads (read_guest_file)
are never asked about.

With no provider added nothing changes: the open and getstat paths are
as before.

Verified: portablekit_io_filter_tests gains nine checks (a file served in
place of one on the memory stick, a file served where there is none,
getstat, no provider asked for a write, a path nobody serves still not
found), on Windows. The disc device is not covered by the test; one game
was run with a provider on its disc BGM files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
