+// A file the host serves at a guest path, in place of the file there or where
+// there is none. PortableKit asks every provider, in the order they were
+// added, at each sceIoOpen and sceIoOpenAsync that only reads, and at
+// sceIoGetstat of a path that does not exist. `path` is "disc0:/" or "ms0:/"
+// followed by the path on that device, '/' separated, with "." and ".."
+// resolved, in the case the game wrote it. `fd` is the descriptor the file
+// there has just been opened as (its bytes are at hand through
+// read_open_file), or 0 when there is no file at that path. The first
+// provider that returns a filter serves the file: the game reads what the
+// filter gives, as with set_file_filter, and a path with no file behind it
+// opens as a file of the filter's bytes alone. Null passes the path on. Called
+// on the emulation thread; a provider that serves nothing must be quick.
+using FileProvider = std::function<std::shared_ptr<FileFilter>(std::string_view path, std::uint32_t fd)>;
+void add_file_provider(FileProvider provider);
